     <h1 class="title" title="Coonoor Hill Station">Coonoor</h1>
     <div class="entry-content">

<p>

<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/INDIAHILLSTATION.INFO/images/south-india-hill-stations/coonoor-hill-station.jpg" title="Coonoor hill station" alt="Coonoor hill station, hill stations in india, north india hill stations, Coonoor" style="width:200px;height:150px" class="thumb alignright"/>


<b>Location:</b> Nilgiri Hills,Tamilnadu.<br />
<b>Significance:</b> Heaven Of Beauty<br />
<b>Altitude:</b> 1800m above sea level.<br />
<b>Climate:</b> Summer 24.3&#176;C, Winter 4.8&#176;C.<br />
<b>Best Time to Visit:</b>  October to May.</p>
<p><b>Coonoor</b> known as a small garden area. Coonoor is the first of the three <b>hill stations in the Nilgiris</b>, Ooty, Kotagiri and Coonoor. Sim Park, with all its natural beauty was built in 1874 with trees and unique plants. Coonoor is a good place for nature lovers. It shines fresh vegetation and landscapes. Coonoor has a number of ideals of green party picnic for the eyes of visitors. Coonoor is a great <b>place for tourists in India</b>. It is characterized by the <b>different varieties of birds</b>. Several species of vultures, eagles and owls, songbirds and bulbuls, thrushes, babblers, larks, cuckoos, robins, and many others act as a new adventure melodious music gives effect to visitors who are accustomed to city noise pollution.</p>

